[2026-09-13 07:46:38] REQ 260913074424-8 START backend=Ollama model=glm-5.3-flash:cloud msgs=16 roles=assistant,tool,assistant,tool,assistant,tool tail=[{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_7u8gcamb","function":{"index":0,"name":"read_task","arguments":{}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[07:45:00] git-commit-tool-guard\n  #+TITLE: git-commit-tool guard -- refuse staging audit/*/cycle.log\n#+FILETAGS: :build:git:guard:\n\n* WHY\n\nc270: continuo's cycle.log (raw transcript, 85MB working tree) was\nre-added to git by the git_commit tool's `git add -A` after a stale\ncheckout resurrected it past its untrack commit (917ff7d9 untracked it\nlaw-22; 03c00b2c re-added it via add -A sweeping). 109 commits carried\n~6.7GiB of raw blob versions before c270's re-untrack. The tool is the\nresurrection vector: any tracked-but-ignored file swept by add -A comes\nback every commit.\n\n* WHAT\n\nModify /root/i.ar/emacs.d/init.d/tools/git/git_commit.el:\niar--tool-git-commit. After the `git add -A` succeeds, check\n`git diff --cached --name-only` for paths matching\n`audit/[^/]+/cycle.log` (and generally: any path the repo's .gitignore\nwould exclude -- `git diff --cached --name-only -- .` vs\n`git ls-files --ignored --exclude-standard --cached`). If a match:\n\n1. Unstage the offending paths: `git rm --cached --quiet <paths>`.\n2. Log a warning line into the commit message or return a Success\n   note mentioning the refused paths, so the agent sees it.\n\nSimplest robust shape: after add -A, run\n`git diff --cached --name-only --diff-filter=A` and intersect with\n`git ls-files --others --ignored --exclude-standard` -- newly-added\nfiles that are gitignored = resurrection. Unstage those. Keep the\ncommit going (do not fail the whole commit).\n\n* TESTS\n\nExtend /root/i.ar/emacs.d/test/test-git-commit.el:\n- fixture repo with .gitignore ignoring a path, a previously-tracked\n  ignored file (simulate: track it, commit, then untrack with\n  git rm --cached but leave the file), modify it, call the tool ->\n  commit succeeds, file NOT re-added (git ls-files shows it absent).\n- normal add still works (existing tests green).\n\n* CONSTRAINTS\n\n- Suite green before push (run ert tests).\n- This is i.ar core .el: allowed (self-modification enabled for aria),\n  but commit separately from personalization repo.\n- Update docs/iar/tools.md per the maintenance rule.\n* STATUS: LANDED 2026-09-13 cycle c273 (aria)\n\ni.ar repo commit dd4118a, pushed to rammstein mirror.  Full suite\n1250/1250 green before push.\n\n* WHAT LANDED\n\n- emacs.d/init.d/tools/git/git_commit.el: new\n  `iar--git-unstage-refused' runs after `git add -A' and before the\n  commit.  Staged paths matching `iar-git-commit-refuse-pattern'\n  (default \"\\\\`audit/.*cycle\\\\.log\\\\'\") are unstaged via\n  `git rm --cached --quiet'; the tool result carries a\n  \"Note: refused to stage ...\" line.  The commit itself never fails.\n- Dated transcripts (cycle-YYYY-MM-DD.log) deliberately do NOT match:\n  belt-discipline artifacts, tracked intentionally via add -f.\n- Tool description updated so agents see the refusal behavior.\n- Tests (test-git-commit.el): refuses-rolling-transcript (fixture =\n  the ACTUAL c270 state: transcript tracked, .gitignore present,\n  transcript grows; guard unstages, commit records the deletion,\n  file survives on disk, README still commits), dated-transcript-\n  still-commits, guard-silent-when-clean.\n- docs/iar/tools.md updated (personalization repo 7436b393).\n\n* TEST-RUNNER NOTE (scar)\n\nrun-tests.sh only loads test-prompt-assembly.el -- the \"suite green\"\nline from run-tests.sh is NOT the full suite.  The full suite is\n`emacs --batch -l test/run-tests.el` (1250 tests, ~8s).  Discovered\nthis cycle when test-git-commit.el silently didn't run under\nrun-tests.sh.\n[t+00:35/60:00 c5/300]"},{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_adn8yux7","function":{"index":0,"name":"execute_code_local","arguments":{"command"