uration\n--\n46-#   watch state, no RECOVERY; sane-window segments (16.0s) ->\n47-#   RECOVERY fires correctly.\n48:# v2.18 (aria cycle 158, 2026-09-10): SEG-TAIL KNOWN_FAULT allowlist\n49-#   (second application of the v2.9 KNOWN_DEAF contract). exterior_1\n50-#   carries a camera-side video-timestamp poison (c151 diagnosis,\n51-#   knowledge/aria/exterior1-timestamp-poison-c151.md) that makes the\n52:#   SEG-TAIL probe flap FAIL/OK depending on which segment is newest.\n53-#   The fault is filed (relay aria-0028, camera reboot = Nacho,\n54-#   physical). Until it lands, every flap pulses the fear organ sev=2\n55-#   on a KNOWN camera-side fault -- alarm fatigue on a real but\n56-#   already-owned signal. Contract (identical to KNOWN_DEAF):\n57:#   known-fault + SEG-TAIL FAIL = watch state (reported, not failed);\n58:#   known-fault + SEG-TAIL OK = RECOVERY event, FAIL loudly (withdraw\n59-#   the flag, update KNOWN_FAULT). A NEW fault on any other camera\n60-#   fails as before. KNOWN_FAULT is a list of camera names.\n61-# v2.17 (aria cycle 151): interior_3 RECOVERED (audio back, live-verified 09:47 UTC 09-10) -- allowlist emptied; it now FAILs if it goes deaf again. v2.16 (aria cycle 150): N-SEGMENT EAR CHECK (3-segment window).\n62-#   The 2026-09-10 03:01Z fleet run FAILed on exterior_3 NO-AUDIO --\n63-#   but the sampled segment (01.07.mp4, 0.79s) was a video-only STUB\n64-#   written during a frigate watchdog restart (00:00:43 fps-limit kill\n--\n386-  # so v2.18's RECOVERY branch (probe OK while flag set) fired a\n387-  # standing FALSE RECOVERY on every run of a poisoned-but-decodable\n388:  # camera (live: 18:04 -03 feeder run, duration 412523s, \"SEG-TAIL\n389-  # RECOVERED\"). Fix: pair the decode with a duration check. Sane\n390-  # ext1 segments are 16.0s; poisoned are >=28h (or transient stubs\n391-  # <6s, which already fail the tail decode). Threshold 60s.\n392-  segdur=$($P exec frigate sh -c \"/usr/lib/ffmpeg/7.0/bin/ffprobe -v error -show_entries