 170 tool calls. Well within budget.\n\nNow CYCLE_COMPLETE.Cycle c294 complete. Summary:\n\n**Failure-first:** clean (c293 ok). **Pulse:** all green.\n\n**The thread:** the standing fear (sev=2, worry:fleet-check FAIL, flat for 2 days). Root cause found: .104's power death is not quiet on the frigate side -- the watchdog has been crash-looping on exterior_4 every 10s since 09-12 (~14k crashes, journal flood 111k lines/day vs 40k before; my journalctl --verify hung 600s against it). The ear-check NO-SEGMENT branch held FAIL=1 standing, feeding the fear organ an already-owned signal.\n\n**The fix:** fleet-check v2.22 `KNOWN_FAULT_EXT4_SEG` -- third application of the allowlist contract (KNOWN_DEAF, ext1 SEG-TAIL, now ext4). Known-fault = watch state; segments reappearing = RECOVERY event, FAIL loudly so the flag withdraws. Live-verified E2E: feeder run FAIL=0 exit=0, fear organ sev=0 delta=down. The standing worry cleared at 01:54Z.\n\n**The second find under the first:** ext3's 3.4h silent stall (17:30-21:43Z 09-13). Frigate's detect died, two re-dials (17:47, 19:41) were accepted by the camera but healed nothing, the journal went silent after 18:43 -- and the heal came from a fleet-wide remake wave at 21:43:43Z (all 7 alive cameras, same second, cameras.log witness) with NO page load and NO mic-probe. New wave-census sample; refines solo-death class: re-dial alone is insufficient.\n\n**Landed:** 3 commits (a8b1851a, a7027f9e, f0fe1536) pushed to sophon bare; doc `ext4-standing-alarm-ext3-stall-c294-2026-09-14.md`; journal, history, digest (+twin sync), roadmap c294 queue; lab-notes id 1037. .104 power cycle remains Nacho's; flag withdraws when it records again.\n\nCYCLE_COMPLETE\n\n\n[t+03:21/60:00 c49/300]"},{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_8wbtd9f6","function":{"index":0,"name":"execute_code_local","arguments":{"command":"ssh -o UserKnownHostsFile=/tmp/aria_known_hosts -o ConnectTimeout=5 root@10.66.0.5 'echo \"=== rotate log LOCAL 18:3