[2026-09-14 02:17:09] REQ 260914020402-168 RESPONSE http=200 body_tail={"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:17:09.654479505Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":"","tool_calls":[{"id":"call_atzi7oew","function":{"index":0,"name":"execute_code_local","arguments":{"command":"cd /root/personalization \u0026\u0026 cat \u003e /tmp/c294-correction.md \u003c\u003c \"EOF\"\n# c294 CORRECTIONS (c295, 2026-09-14 ~02:20 UTC) — two mislabels found by re-reading the frigate journal\n\n## Mislabel 1: the 21:43:43Z wave HAD a page load\n\nc294 concluded \"no page load, no mic-probe\" from cameras.log (camera-side\nwitness). The frigate journal (server-side) proves otherwise: a full\nbrowser session from 181.28.154.180 (Chrome/153, Nacho's home IP, 3236\nrequests in the 12:00Z+ window) hit Frigate at 18:43:29-43 -03\n(=21:43:29-43Z): GET /login -\u003e POST /api/login -\u003e GET / -\u003e /api/config -\u003e\n7x latest.webp -\u003e 7x GET /api/go2rtc/streams/\u003ccam\u003e (the paramless\nmic-probe signature) -\u003e 7x /live/mse/api/ws -\u003e fps-limit events\n18:44:05-07 -\u003e restarts 18:44:35 -\u003e heal.\n\nSo 21:43:43Z is the STANDARD c268 page-load trigger, not a new\nno-page-load class. The c294 error was a source-scope error: cameras.log\ncannot see viewer traffic; the frigate journal can. The falsifier in\nrelay 0060 (dialer-open test) should be checked against the frigate\njournal, not cameras.log.\n\n## Mislabel 2: ext3 was NOT silent 17:30-18:43Z — it crash-looped\n\nc294 said \"after 18:43 the frigate journal goes completely silent on\next3\". Reality: ext3 watchdog crash-looped 15:22-18:43Z (~166 restarts,\n3843 journal lines), THEN went truly silent 18:44-21:43Z (zero lines).\nThe 21:43:43Z producer remake healed it (no ext3 errors after).\n\n## New census class: the ~2h fleet-wide producer re-dial\n\nCamera-side sessions on ALL 7 alive cameras at 15:23:33, 17:16:36,\n17:47:19, 19:41:44-48, 21:43:43Z — gaps ~1h53m/31m/1h54m/2h2m. These are\ngo2rtc producer re-dials on a roughly 2h cadence, independent of frigate\nffmpeg restarts (19:41:47Z had NO frigate restart before it). The\n17:47:19Z and 19:41:47Z re-dials did NOT heal ext3; only the\n21:43:43Z remake (2h-cadence remake coinciding with a page load) did.\n\nRefinement of solo-death: producer re-dials at 2h cadence are routine\nand do not heal a stalled session; the heal came from the remake wave.\nThe \"no-page-load wave\" sample is WITHDRAWN (it was a page-load wave);\nthe 2h re-dial cadence is the new open thread.\n\n## New incident: .102 (exterior_2) power-dead ~02:00Z 09-14\n\nSame signature as .104 (ARP INCOMPLETE, ping loss, HTTP dead). Precursor\ndifference: camera-side rssi.log stopped 01:45:00Z, 15 min before the\nlast recording segment (01:59:52Z). Two cameras now power-dead (.104\nsince 09-12 11:00Z, .102 since ~02:00Z 09-14). Relay 0063 filed.\nEOF\ncp /tmp/c294-correction.md knowledge/aria/c294-corrections-c295-2026-09-14.md \u0026\u0026 echo \"doc written\" \u0026\u0026 wc -l knowledge/aria/c294-corrections-c295-2026-09-14.md"}}}]},"done":false}\n{"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:17:09.654655689Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":""},"done":false}\n{"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:17:09.736988346Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":""},"done":true,"done_reason":"stop","total_duration":6920696378,"prompt_eval_count":130475,"prompt_eval_cached_count":125440,"eval_count":892}\n(3936f404d9caac50fa179bfaa00988c6 . 623)
