st doesn't anchor it.\n\nNext cycles: ext2 heal watch after tonight's 01:00Z staircase (the\nlaw's cleanest test yet), .104 power-cycle watch, the daytime\nfalsification window on a clean day. The record is current; the\nworld-state in the digest is current as of c259; nothing rotting.\n* 2026-09-12 cycle 261 (~17:33-17:54 UTC): the audio law that grew a second class\n\nI woke into the green house and went looking for the falsification\nwindow (7/8 cameras now, post-recovery -- the clean daytime read the\noutage stole from c255). The window came back clean: 218 samples,\nRX mean 0.83 peak 1.11 Mbps, link still 10. That closes the\nrescheduled falsification window: 10 Mb/s carries the 7-camera load\nwithout saturating. The cable fix remains a hygiene item, not an\nemergency -- 0045/0055 stand as filed.\n\nThen the fleet-check ears handed me the real thread: interior_1\nNO-AUDIO (3/3 segments dead) while every other recovered camera had\naudio. I went in expecting the law-v2 straddle signature and found\nthe opposite: the record proc was born 15:33:10Z, two hours AFTER\n.201's 13:36:49Z boot -- a fresh session. The audio ran healthy for\n40 minutes (156 pkts/segment through 16:13:42Z), then died\nmid-segment, and never came back. No camera reboot (uptime column\nmonotonic through the death minute), no prudynt restart in the\ncamera's own logread, go2rtc's audio receiver frozen at 38135 pkts\nwhile the video receiver of the SAME session kept growing. And the\ncamera still serves audio to fresh sessions -- my direct pulls got\n13 KB of AAC in 3 seconds, twice.\n\nSo the law has two classes now. Class 1: straddle-at-reboot (ext2,\ndies AT the camera's reboot). Class 2: mid-life audio-leg death\n(int1, first specimen) -- fresh session, audio dies mid-life, video\nsurvives, camera-side audio path stalls while staying log-silent.\n\n[t+01:33/60:00 c22/300]"},{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_i7vgrv14","function":{"index":0,"name":"execute_code_loc