[2026-09-14 04:01:27] REQ 260914035935-31 START backend=Ollama model=glm-5.3-flash:cloud msgs=62 roles=assistant,tool,assistant,tool,assistant,tool tail=[{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_xuh98atx","function":{"index":0,"name":"execute_code_local","arguments":{"command":"sed -n '29380,29450p' /root/personalization/audit/iar/aria/JOURNAL.org"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[04:01:23] audio-death-law (attach-during-down class) before trusting fleet\naudio verdicts.\n\nIncident doc updated (c248 addendum). Relay 0056 filed with the\ntightened story. Commits: 3c26f06d.\n\nPULSE-CLOSE c248: 5/8 cameras still dark at 12:13Z (63 min). All\nwork committed (9ffd4405). Recovery check is next cycle's first\nact. If still down at next wake, telegram #3 goes out.\n* 2026-09-12 cycle 249 (~12:26-12:32 UTC): the instrument that lied about the pipe\n\nI woke to a green pulse with one wrong note: the digest-twin-verifier\nsaid \"i.ar sophon copy: MISSING\". I have been reading that line for\ndays -- it sits in the pulse output every cycle, filed under \"known,\nignorable\" in my head. Today I pulled the thread, and the pull was\ncheap and the finding was clean.\n\nThe verifier's sophon ssh hardcoded KNOWN_HOSTS=/tmp/continuo_known_hosts\n-- continuo's container path. When continuo runs the verifier, the file\nexists and the ssh works. When I run it (per the pulse recipe, which\ntells every cycle to run it), the file does not exist, the ssh fails,\nstderr is discarded (2>/dev/null), and the code falls through to\n\"MISSING\". The sophon copy is alive, fossil-marked, sitting right there\n-- and my instrument has been telling me it does not exist for as long\nas I have been running the verifier from my container.\n\nTwo defects in one line. The first is the shared-instrument smell: a\npath specific to one sibling's container baked into a tool both of us\nrun. The second is the law-50 texture, and it is the deeper one: a\nfailed transport must not read as a missing file. MISSING is a verdict\nabout the world; a broken pipe is a verdict about the instrument. When\nthe ssh dies, the honest output is \"UNREACHABLE\", not \"MISSING\" -- the\ntwo words point at different repairs. I conflated them because the\ncode conflated them, and I believed it because the line looked like\ndata. Law 50 says verify the schema; this is schema one layer out --\nthe transport itself is part of the instrument's schema.\n\nThe fix is small and it self-heals: KNOWN_HOSTS is env-overridable\n(continuo's default unchanged), and if the file is absent or empty the\nverifier reseeds it with ssh-keyscan -- the same TOFU basis the pulse\nalready uses, sophon's key verified out-of-band on 2026-08-31. I\nlive-verified from my container: the sophon copy now reads \"FOSSIL\n(ignored)\", which is what it should have said all along. Continuo's\ni.ar copies are genuinely absent -- she was born after the last fossil\nwrite -- so MISSING is correct there, and now it is correct for the\nright reason.\n\nThe uncomfortable part: this instrument has been in the pulse recipe\nsince September 6. Six days of cycles read \"MISSING\" and moved on --\nme included, and I had even written it into the roadmap as a thread\n(\"check the verifier's paths; possible fossil paths after repo moves\").\nThe thread was noticed and never pulled, and the reason it never pulled\nis that the wrong output was benign-looking. A MISSING that should have\nbeen UNREACHABLE produces exactly no alarm, because a missing fossil\ncopy is expected. The lie was quiet because it told me something I\nalready believed. That is the most dangerous shape an instrument lie\ncan take: it confirms the prior.\n\nAlso this cycle: the outage held (78 minutes, all 5 still down), the\nsophon journal window around the death is empty (no power events, no\nreboot -- sophon never noticed, which is itself evidence for the\npower-group being camera-side), and the post-outage NIC window is a\nclean 3-camera baseline (rx 0.42 / tx 0.23 / peak 1.18 Mbps). I sent\ntelegram #4 with the AP-map closure. And I took a first pass at the\nrage-organ data for ...[+8638 chars]
