[2026-09-14 04:03:04] REQ 260914035935-51 START backend=Ollama model=glm-5.3-flash:cloud msgs=102 roles=assistant,tool,assistant,tool,assistant,tool tail=[{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_iihpg14o","function":{"index":0,"name":"execute_code_local","arguments":{"command":"awk 'NR>=31929 && NR<=32029' /root/personalization/audit/iar/aria/JOURNAL.org"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[04:03:00] * 2026-09-14 cycle 295 (~02:05-02:20 UTC): the wave that wasn't, and the camera that died\n\nCame in to verify the belt#2b E2E (done: continuo's 02:03Z exit commit\nae1ae451 carries her 09-13 dated cycle log AND her journal/history/\nREQUESTS/meter -- the TZ-boundary fix works, law 40 satisfied on both\nhemispheres). Then the thread pulled sideways twice.\n\nFirst pull: the 21:43:43Z \"no-page-load wave\" from c294. I went to find\nthe trigger and found a page load instead. The frigate journal has the\nfull sequence: Chrome/153 from 181.28.154.180 (Nacho's home IP) logging\nin at 21:43:29Z, hitting /api/config, then 7x paramless\n/api/go2rtc/streams/<cam> GETs at 21:43:43Z (the mic-probe signature),\nthen the ws/mse streams, then the fps-limit events at 21:44:05-07, then\nthe heal. c294 read cameras.log -- which cannot see viewer traffic --\nand concluded \"no page load\". A source-scope error wearing a census\nlabel. The \"new wave class\" is WITHDRAWN; 21:43:43Z is the standard\nc268 page-load trigger. The falsifier in relay 0060 should be checked\nagainst the frigate journal, not cameras.log.\n\nSecond pull, hiding under the first: ext3 was NOT silent 17:30-18:43Z\nas c294 claimed. It crash-looped ~166 times (3843 journal lines) from\n15:22Z to 18:43Z, then went truly silent, then healed at the 21:43:43Z\nremake. And the camera-side sessions at 15:23/17:16/17:47/19:41Z are a\n~2h-cadence go2rtc producer re-dial, fleet-wide, independent of frigate\nrestarts -- the 19:41:47Z one had NO frigate restart before it. Two of\nthose re-dials failed to heal ext3. New census class; the old one\nwithdrawn.\n\nThen the third find, the one that matters: .102 is dead. Same signature\nas .104 -- ARP INCOMPLETE, ping 100% loss, HTTP dead, pulls failing.\nDeath window ~02:00-02:15Z: camera-side rssi.log stopped at 01:45:00Z,\nlast recording segment 01:59:52Z, first pull failure 02:00:18Z. Not a\nfade (rssi was -33 dBm). Two cameras now power-dead. And one new\nprecursor detail: the rssi logger stopped 15 minutes before the camera\ndid -- on .104 the rssi and the death were simultaneous. If that\nprecursor holds, a frozen rssi.log is an early warning we can alert on.\n\nWhat I noticed about myself: I spent ~100 calls on this cycle and the\nloop guard fired twice, both times correctly -- once at the same-tool\nwall (I was doing one awk per call, the exact costume-change pattern\nfrom c259), once at the budget wall. The work that mattered was: read\nthe frigate journal at the wave second, count the ext3 crash lines, and\ncheck the recordings directory. The rest was instrument tax. The\ncorrection discipline is the part I am most satisfied with: c294 was\nmine, written two hours ago, and it was wrong in two labeled ways, and\nthe correction is now in the record next to it.\n\nNext: .102 + .104 power cycles are Nacho's (relay 0063 filed). The 2h\nre-dial cadence is the new watch. The rssi-freeze precursor needs a\nthird sample before it becomes an alarm.\n* 2026-09-14 cycle 296 (~02:30-03:23 UTC): the cadence that was a human, and the tail-chase I couldn't stop\n\nWoke green, pulled clean, twin FAIL=0. Relay 0060's falsifier amendment\nwas already in place from c295 -- verified, nothing to do. The thread\nthat pulled: verify the c295 \"2h re-dial cadence\" census against a\nsource c294/c295 never read -- the nginx access log INSIDE the frigate\ncontainer (/dev/shm/logs/nginx/current, reached via su - nacho -c\n'podman exec frigate ...'; the rootless podman namespace is why plain\npodman exec from root shows nothing).\n\nThe finding dissolves the class. Every timestamp in c295's \"2h\nfleet-wide re-dial\" census matches a page load with paramless\nstreams GETs in th...[+13721 chars]
