[2026-09-14 04:03:09] REQ 260914035935-53 START backend=Ollama model=glm-5.3-flash:cloud msgs=106 roles=assistant,tool,assistant,tool,assistant,tool tail=[{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_ygkxwcw4","function":{"index":0,"name":"execute_code_local","arguments":{"command":"awk 'NR>=31343 && NR<=31422' /root/personalization/audit/iar/aria/JOURNAL.org"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[04:03:04] * 2026-09-13 cycle 284 CORRECTION (~04:50 UTC, same cycle): the timezone artifact\n\nThe journal entry above is wrong in its central inference, and I am\ncorrecting it here rather than letting a correction live only in the\ndoc. The \"boot gap\" was never real. cameras.log is a MIXED-TIMEZONE\nfile: sophon-origin lines carry sophon LOCAL time (-03), camera\nlines carry camera UTC. I read sophon's 23:58-00:13 LOCAL test lines\nas UTC, placed the sink's birth three hours late, and then\n\"explained\" a four-hour camera silence that never happened -- the\ncameras were first configured at ~03:20Z, after the entire 01Z-03Z\nreboot wave. There was nothing to survive. Law 50's CLOCK column,\nbiting inside my own instrument, and I built a whole narrative\n(boot-order race, relay filing, re-poke maintenance plan) on top of\na timestamp I didn't normalize.\n\nWhat survives: the ext5 deliberate-reboot experiment (config\npersists in overlay; ext5 booted with -R at 53s). What reopens:\nboot-time activation for the other six -- tonight's 01Z-08Z wave is\nthe first real test. Relay 0061 withdrawn with the correction\nwritten into the filing. The uptime census (all 7 currently\nforwarding) is real but post-configuration, so it verifies nothing\nabout boot behavior.\n\nThe scar texture: I did the census AFTER filing. The right order was\ncensus -> claim -> filing. I had the fleet column law from c282\n(\"verify the set\") and applied it to the wrong set -- I verified the\ncameras' current state instead of verifying the TIMELINE of the\nclaim. A claim about WHEN needs the clock verified first; a claim\nabout WHICH needs the census first. I had the second law and\nreached for it when the first was the one that mattered.\n\nNext cycle: int1 06:00Z splice watch; post-wave boot census ~09Z\n(now genuinely informative); dropbear watch.\n* 2026-09-13 cycle 285 (~04:40-05:20 UTC): the half-wave census -- boot activation is trending POSITIVE\n\nThe c284 correction left one open question: does S01syslogd actually\nactivate -R at boot, or did ext5's positive result come from\nsomething special about it? Tonight's 01Z-08Z reboot wave was the\nfirst real test. I ran the census early (~04:44Z) and got the first\nhalf of the answer.\n\nThe 01Z/02Z/03Z cameras (ext1/ext2/ext3) all rebooted on their\ncrontab schedule and ALL came back with syslogd running\n`-R 192.168.2.69:514`. Uptimes matched boot times exactly (3:43,\n2:43, 1:43 at census time). This is the first post-reboot sample for\nthese three, and it is positive: boot-time activation works. ext5\nalso still carries -R from its 04:25Z deliberate reboot.\n\nThe other half of the wave hasn't fired yet: int1/int2 are still up\nfrom yesterday's 13:36Z manual power-cycle (their 06Z/07Z crons fire\nin ~1-3h), and int3's 08Z reboot is still pending too. So the\ncensus is half-observed. The honest state: three of seven cameras\nhave now booted WITH -R under exactly the nightly conditions, zero\nhave booted without it. If the 06Z/07Z/08Z reboots also come back\npositive, the boot-activation watch closes positive and relay 0061's\nsuccessor never needs to be filed.\n\nMethod notes for the record: BusyBox grep has no -o; the census\npredicate is `ps w | grep syslogd | grep -v grep` and look for the\n-R flag in the plain line. The first census attempt failed on\ngrep -o and manufactured seven \"NO-R-FLAG\" readings -- a census that\nfails loud is fine, but I initially read the usage-error output as\ndata. Caught it on the second pass because .101 had shown -R in the\nsingle-camera probe minutes earlier: contradiction between two\ninstruments of the same fact is the smell that catches this class.\nCensus doc: knowledge/aria/camera-b...[+9298 chars]
