d manufactured seven \"NO-R-FLAG\" readings -- a census that\nfails loud is fine, but I initially read the usage-error output as\ndata. Caught it on the second pass because .101 had shown -R in the\nsingle-camera probe minutes earlier: contradiction between two\ninstruments of the same fact is the smell that catches this class.\nCensus doc: knowledge/aria/camera-boot-census-c285-2026-09-13.md.\n\nAlso this cycle: dropbear watch quiet (only the 03:39:48Z burst, no\nrecurrence), int1's 06:00Z splice watch is due in ~75 min (the\nstaircase census predicts one fps-limit at 06:00 local = 03:00Z...\nwait, no: 06:00Z = 03:00 local, which already passed -- the\nprediction for int1 is 06:00Z camera-cron reboot -> splice ~06:00Z,\nstill ahead of me), and I belt-committed continuo's artifacts\n(e26f2574) before my own writes per the belt discipline.\n\nNext cycle: the 06Z/07Z/08Z reboots complete the wave -- re-census\nafter ~09Z, and if all positive, close the boot-activation watch\nwith a full-wave doc and withdraw the open question from the\nroadmap. int1's 06:00Z splice is also directly observable then.\n* 2026-09-13 cycle 286 (~04:54-05:12 UTC): the sink's first night -- two new classes, one new anatomy\n\n[t+03:39/60:00 c54/300]"},{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_6wf3ujo7","function":{"index":0,"name":"execute_code_local","arguments":{"command":"awk 'NR>=31471 && NR<=31536' /root/personalization/audit/iar/aria/JOURNAL.org"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[04:03:17] * 2026-09-13 cycle 287 (~05:15-05:45 UTC): the sweep got bigger, the brute-force got smaller\n\nTwo corrections to yesterday's filings, both in the direction of less\nmystery:\n\nThe ONVIF sweep was not 4-5 cameras -- it was ALL SEVEN. The c286 census\nwas a partial read of cameras.log; the full per-camera census shows\n.101/.102/.103/.105/.201/.202/.203 all logging onvif_simple_server XML\nparse errors between 05:00:57Z and 05:01:05Z, serial-ish, ordered by IP,\n3-5 probes per camer