n failed to identify the caller. Dashboard,\nfleet-check, rage/fear organs, fleet-feed, pullers -- all exonerated. No\nsophon journal entries at the time. So: something on the LAN swept the\ncameras with malformed ONVIF probes at 02:00:58 local, and I don't know\nwhat. Combined with the dropbear burst at 03:39:48Z (also camera-directed,\nalso unattributed), that's two scanning events in 80 minutes. Relay 0062\nfiled -- Nacho may recognize a PTZ app or HA integration; if he doesn't,\nit's an attribution problem worth his eyes.\n\nThe scar of the cycle: I burned 100 tool calls on this investigation,\nmostly in big batched ssh blocks that were fine, but the go2rtc\nconsumer-check at the end tripped the same-tool warning. The batch\ndiscipline held until the tail. Also: my first \"IP map\" in this cycle's\nhead was wrong (.103=ext1) and I caught it only when the backchannel\nwitness didn't match ext1's clean recordings -- the contradiction-between-\ninstruments law again, this time catching a map, not a reading.\n\nWhat the sink proved: backchannel configs, encoder clog, onvif probes --\nthree camera-side witness classes that frigate cannot see. First night,\ntwo new classes. The instrument paid for itself twice.\n\nNext cycle: int1 06:00Z splice watch (due ~06:00Z), full-wave boot census\n~09Z, ONVIF recurrence watch (tcpdump armed in the task), audio/video\ndivergence backfill census.\n* 2026-09-13 cycle 287 (~05:15-05:45 UTC): the sweep got bigger, the brute-force got smaller\n\n[t+03:44/60:00 c56/300]"},{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_7jr56tkr","function":{"index":0,"name":"execute_code_local","arguments":{"command":"awk 'NR>=31471 && NR<=31536' /root/personalization/audit/iar/aria/JOURNAL.org | tail -30; echo \"=== 288 ===\"; awk 'NR>=31536 && NR<=31594' /root/personalization/audit/iar/aria/JOURNAL.org | head -55"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[04:03:21] census discipline working -- yesterday's numbers were honest-but-partial,\nand the