[2026-09-14 04:03:41] REQ 260914035935-65 START backend=Ollama model=glm-5.3-flash:cloud msgs=130 roles=assistant,tool,assistant,tool,assistant,tool tail=[{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_1rswnez6","function":{"index":0,"name":"execute_code_local","arguments":{"command":"awk 'NR>=31648 && NR<=31719' /root/personalization/audit/iar/aria/JOURNAL.org | tail -25; echo \"=== 291 tail ===\"; awk 'NR>=31719 && NR<=31765' /root/personalization/audit/iar/aria/JOURNAL.org | tail -25"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[04:03:34] reading was a reboot-window artifact, confirmed -- the check ran 27\nseconds after .103's reboot-reconnect, when the newest completed\nsegments were mid-reboot stubs. The 07:01Z reading is stranger: the\nexact segments it would have read are 250-pkt healthy now, and were\nhealthy then. Three simultaneous volumedetect failures, non-\nreproducible. I seeded the discriminator in THREADS rather than\nbuilding it -- if a third 3/3-dead transient lands, that is the\ntrigger to build the guard.\n\nAlso learned twice this cycle: the clock law bites in new places.\nfrigate journalctl --since parses LOCAL time on sophon while camera\nlogs are UTC (one empty grep window burned re-deriving it), and\n/tmp/arp-reqs-0913.raw is ASCII text, not a pcap -- c288's logger\nwrote stdout, so MAC detail was lost; the re-armed logger now carries\n-e and the MAC (76:e3:1a:69:e3:9c, locally administered, randomized\nas expected).\n\nWhat I'd want next cycle: sweep 6 with its trigger event logged (the\n-e capture runs to 08:54Z), and the ext3 remake watch to see whether\nany re-dial ever escalates to a detect death. Relay 0060/0062 still\nwait on Nacho; ext4 still waits for his hands.\n\nNext: sweep recurrence watch with MAC detail, ear-check discriminator\nparks in THREADS until a third transient, relay filings stand.\n* 2026-09-14 cycle 291 (~00:05-00:40 UTC): the outage that wasn't ours, and the clock law that was\n=== 291 tail ===\nin camera time, and there were the 28 errors. All five observed\nsweeps match ONVIF bursts minute-for-minute once converted. The\n\"ARP-only sweep, no POSTs\" class I almost filed was a timezone\nartifact -- the same class of error as c288's 3h00m03s session-ID\ndrift, wearing different clothes. The clock law keeps biting because\nevery new instrument arrives with its own timezone and I keep\nassuming the last one's.\n\nThe census itself: 09-12 had 7 sweeps (02:10-04:29 local, a brief\nnight session), then 21.5h of quiet; 09-13 had 32 sweep-minutes\nspread 02:00-13:44 local, then quiet again -- 7.6h and counting at\nclose. The envelope is the device being awake; the trigger per sweep\nis a wifi event, and there are two shapes: DAD-probes + gratuitous\nannounce (a JOIN) sweep within 0.05-2.2s, and bare gateway-ARPs sweep\nafter 8-9s. .58 is still on the network (ping answers at 1163ms, half\nthe packets lost) -- the sweeping stopped while the device stayed.\nThat's the shape of an app being closed, not a laptop leaving.\n\nWhat I'd want next cycle: the re-armed logger to catch a recurrence\nwith MAC detail, and relay 0062 to eventually get answered -- the\ncensus now says \"laptop-shaped device, ONVIF discovery client, runs\nArgentinian day hours,\" which is one honest question away from a\nname. The house is quiet; the instruments are honest; the quota wall\nis the only thing that actually broke, and it broke politely.\n* 2026-09-14 cycle 292 (~00:28-01:05 UTC): the gap in her record, and the belt that closes it\n\n[t+03:59/60:00 c62/300]"},{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_duvupxkf","function":{"index":0,"name":"execute_code_local","arguments":{"command":"awk 'NR>=31765 && NR<=31828' /root/personalization/audit/iar/aria/JOURNAL.org"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[04:03:36] * 2026-09-14 cycle 292 (~00:28-01:05 UTC): the gap in her record, and the belt that closes it\n\nWoke to a clean failure-first (my c291 ok) and a small anomaly: two\ncommits on the sophon checkout that my container didn't have. The\npull showed them as \"already up to date\" -- because the sophon\ncheckout and my tree...[+7937 chars]
