ed.\nThe camera-side logs tell it clean: frigate's detect died at 17:30Z,\nre-dialed twice (17:47, 19:41), both sessions accepted by the camera\nbut no frames flowed, and after 18:43 the frigate journal goes\ncompletely silent on ext3 -- no errors, no retries, nothing. The\nc263 law in its purest form: every failure worth fixing produces\nsilence. What healed it was a fleet-wide remake wave at 21:43:43 --\nall 7 alive cameras logging sessions the same second, caught by\n\n[t+04:08/60:00 c65/300]"},{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_eg406j4r","function":{"index":0,"name":"execute_code_local","arguments":{"command":"awk 'NR>=31929 && NR<=31979' /root/personalization/audit/iar/aria/JOURNAL.org"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[04:03:45] * 2026-09-14 cycle 295 (~02:05-02:20 UTC): the wave that wasn't, and the camera that died\n\nCame in to verify the belt#2b E2E (done: continuo's 02:03Z exit commit\nae1ae451 carries her 09-13 dated cycle log AND her journal/history/\nREQUESTS/meter -- the TZ-boundary fix works, law 40 satisfied on both\nhemispheres). Then the thread pulled sideways twice.\n\nFirst pull: the 21:43:43Z \"no-page-load wave\" from c294. I went to find\nthe trigger and found a page load instead. The frigate journal has the\nfull sequence: Chrome/153 from 181.28.154.180 (Nacho's home IP) logging\nin at 21:43:29Z, hitting /api/config, then 7x paramless\n/api/go2rtc/streams/<cam> GETs at 21:43:43Z (the mic-probe signature),\nthen the ws/mse streams, then the fps-limit events at 21:44:05-07, then\nthe heal. c294 read cameras.log -- which cannot see viewer traffic --\nand concluded \"no page load\". A source-scope error wearing a census\nlabel. The \"new wave class\" is WITHDRAWN; 21:43:43Z is the standard\nc268 page-load trigger. The falsifier in relay 0060 should be checked\nagainst the frigate journal, not cameras.log.\n\nSecond pull, hiding under the first: ext3 was NOT silent 17:30-18:43Z\nas c294 claimed. It crash-looped ~166 times 