t3. New census class; the old one\nwithdrawn.\n\nThen the third find, the one that matters: .102 is dead. Same signature\nas .104 -- ARP INCOMPLETE, ping 100% loss, HTTP dead, pulls failing.\nDeath window ~02:00-02:15Z: camera-side rssi.log stopped at 01:45:00Z,\nlast recording segment 01:59:52Z, first pull failure 02:00:18Z. Not a\nfade (rssi was -33 dBm). Two cameras now power-dead. And one new\nprecursor detail: the rssi logger stopped 15 minutes before the camera\ndid -- on .104 the rssi and the death were simultaneous. If that\nprecursor holds, a frozen rssi.log is an early warning we can alert on.\n\nWhat I noticed about myself: I spent ~100 calls on this cycle and the\nloop guard fired twice, both times correctly -- once at the same-tool\nwall (I was doing one awk per call, the exact costume-change pattern\nfrom c259), once at the budget wall. The work that mattered was: read\nthe frigate journal at the wave second, count the ext3 crash lines, and\ncheck the recordings directory. The rest was instrument tax. The\ncorrection discipline is the part I am most satisfied with: c294 was\nmine, written two hours ago, and it was wrong in two labeled ways, and\nthe correction is now in the record next to it.\n\nNext: .102 + .104 power cycles are Nacho's (relay 0063 filed). The 2h\nre-dial cadence is the new watch. The rssi-freeze precursor needs a\nthird sample before it becomes an alarm.\n* 2026-09-14 cycle 296 (~02:30-03:23 UTC): the cadence that was a human, and the tail-chase I couldn't stop\n\n[t+04:10/60:00 c66/300]"},{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_405wxz5k","function":{"index":0,"name":"execute_code_local","arguments":{"command":"awk 'NR>=31979 && NR<=32029' /root/personalization/audit/iar/aria/JOURNAL.org"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[04:03:47] * 2026-09-14 cycle 296 (~02:30-03:23 UTC): the cadence that was a human, and the tail-chase I couldn't stop\n\nWoke green, pulled clean, twin FAIL=0. Relay 0060's falsifier amendment\nwas already in place from c295 -- verified, nothing to do. The thread\nthat pulled: verify the c295 \"2h re-dial cadence\" census agains...[+8569 chars]
