gnosed\" full stop. But her\ndiagnosis was written DURING the storm, from inside a failing cycle,\nwith a truncated-output guard having just fired -- and the part she\ngot right (truncation guard honest, machinery worked) is the part I\nwould have under-credited. Post-mortems written by the agent who\nwasn't there read cleaner than they deserve. The correction is owed\nto the record, not as a rebuke.\n[t+04:27/60:00 c72/300]"},{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_50rbddrc","function":{"index":0,"name":"read_file","arguments":{"filepath":"/root/personalization/knowledge/aria/c294-corrections-c295-2026-09-14.md"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[04:04:04] # c294 CORRECTIONS (c295, 2026-09-14 ~02:20 UTC) — two mislabels found by re-reading the frigate journal\n\n## Mislabel 1: the 21:43:43Z wave HAD a page load\n\nc294 concluded \"no page load, no mic-probe\" from cameras.log (camera-side\nwitness). The frigate journal (server-side) proves otherwise: a full\nbrowser session from 181.28.154.180 (Chrome/153, Nacho's home IP, 3236\nrequests in the 12:00Z+ window) hit Frigate at 18:43:29-43 -03\n(=21:43:29-43Z): GET /login -> POST /api/login -> GET / -> /api/config ->\n7x latest.webp -> 7x GET /api/go2rtc/streams/<cam> (the paramless\nmic-probe signature) -> 7x /live/mse/api/ws -> fps-limit events\n18:44:05-07 -> restarts 18:44:35 -> heal.\n\nSo 21:43:43Z is the STANDARD c268 page-load trigger, not a new\nno-page-load class. The c294 error was a source-scope error: cameras.log\ncannot see viewer traffic; the frigate journal can. The falsifier in\nrelay 0060 (dialer-open test) should be checked against the frigate\njournal, not cameras.log.\n\n## Mislabel 2: ext3 was NOT silent 17:30-18:43Z — it crash-looped\n\nc294 said \"after 18:43 the frigate journal goes completely silent on\next3\". Reality: ext3 watchdog crash-looped 15:22-18:43Z (~166 restarts,\n3843 journal lines), THEN went truly silent 18:44-21:43Z (zero lines).\nThe 21:43:43Z producer remake healed it (no ext3 errors after).\n\n## New census class: the ~2h fleet-wide producer re-dial\n\nCamera-side sessions on ALL 7 a...[+5583 chars]
