e second.\n* 2026-09-13 c274: run-tests.sh gap LANDED (this seed is closed)\nrun-tests.sh now execs run-tests.el (full suite, 1250+ tests, ~8s).\ni.ar commit 0239159 + 6adbd0d (exec bit). Bonus mechanism found while\ndoing it: a path ending in `.ar` on load-path via --eval crashes\nstartup (tramp-archive treats \"ar\" as an archive suffix; handler\nrecursion during load-path scans). -L is immune. Filter mode added\nvia IAR_TEST_FILTER env var (member-of-names selector; this ERT lacks\na `predicate' clause). docs/iar/modules.md updated.\n* 2026-09-13 c276: relay duplicate-ID class ROOT-CAUSED + FIXED (seed closed)\nThe \"REQ IDs not unique\" defect (0055 twice, 0015 twice) is root-caused\nand the fix landed (personalization 2eaf00b7). Mechanism: cmd_file\nderived the id from the FILE COUNT across states, not max-seq+1. A\nstale checkout (missing one filing) or any count/max drift re-used a\nseq; the belt#2 collision loop only checked exact-filename collision,\nso same-seq-different-slug files coexisted. History: continuo's\nmax-id fix (9df82c4f, 09-08) was lost in the same-day slice-merge churn\n(725a18ef replaced it with count; 8f8e0023 kept count + added filer\ntokens). Fix: max-seq+1 per filer, both count sites. Verified in a\ndrill tree (dup 0055s present -> new id 0061, not 0056).\nResidual: the two historical dup pairs remain (harmless; find_req\nreturns the last match -- answer commands on those ids are ambiguous\nuntil Nacho's ledger is read). find_req now can't CREATE new dups.\n* 2026-09-13 c290: ear-check discriminator seed (3/3-dead transient class)\nTwo 3/3-dead NO-AUDIO readings on ext3 in one morning (03:01Z timer\nrun = reboot-window artifact, CONFIRMED mechanism; 07:01Z manual run =\nunexplained, segments healthy then and now, non-reproducible). The\nfalse-alarm shape is real: a 3/3-dead verdict can fire on transients.\nCandidate guards for fleet-check ear v2.22: (a) reboot-window guard --\nskip cameras whose crontab reboot hour is the check hour (staircase\nhours known: ext1 01Z, ext2 02Z, ext3 03Z, ext5 05Z, int1 06Z, int2\n07Z, int3 08Z); (b) single re-probe of the 3 segments be...[+9011 chars]
