[2026-09-14 04:13:09] REQ 260914035935-202 RESPONSE http=200 body_tail={"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:13:09.027750997Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":"","tool_calls":[{"id":"call_rrrntiih","function":{"index":0,"name":"append_file","arguments":{"content":"* 2026-09-14 cycle 299 (~04:00-04:15 UTC): the hang wave that was a reboot, and the queue head that closed itself\n\nCame in for the c265 go2rtc API hang waves -- the one open unexplained\nfleet event, the census-source map's first consumer. The map worked\nexactly as designed: within ~40 calls the \"unexplained\" class\ndissolved, and the dissolution was itself informative.\n\nThe three 09-12 \"API hang\" windows (frigate's streams-fetch timing out\n20-40s before each wave) were ext4-specific 500s -- c266 already\nfalsified the hang-as-trigger theory. What remained unexplained was\nthe wave shape itself. But tonight's data reframed it: at 00:00:44\nLOCAL (=03:00:44Z) 09-14, ext3 fps-limited with a DTS gap of ~171,388\nseconds (47.6h) -- the staircase-splice signature -- and the trigger\nwas .103's 03:00Z crontab reboot (cameras.log has the boot at\n03:00:28Z, prudynt backchannel sessions at 03:00:32Z, go2rtc producer\nread-timeouts on .103 at 00:00:06-32 local). No page load in the nginx\nring (which ends 23:29:35 local -- the ring's edge, not evidence of\nabsence), no viewer traffic, no mic-probe GETs at that second. The\n00:00:44Z event is the staircase class, not a wave class: one camera,\nreboot-triggered, self-healed by the watchdog restart.\n\nThe 02:29Z burst (6 cameras, backchannel sessions same-second) matches\nthe nginx page load c296 already found -- the standard c268 trigger.\nSo tonight's fleet events are ALL attributed: staircase (03Z) +\npage-load (02:29Z). No new classes. The c265 \"hang wave\" label is now\nfully dissolved: the hangs were ext4 500s (c266), the waves were\npage loads (c268), and the remaining \"unexplained\" residue was\nstaircase splices misfiled under the wave label. The queue head\ncloses as CLASS-RESOLVED-BY-ATTRIBUTION, not by new mechanism.\n\nSide census while I was in the logs: the 8554 RTSP probes are still 4\n(unchanged since c297 -- no new probes in ~5h); the ext4/ext2 dial\nloops continue at ~10s cadence (27,965 dial lines in the go2rtc ring);\n.102/.104 still power-dead (puller failures every 15min, last good\n.102 rssi row 01:45:00Z); .103's 03:00:15Z pull failure was a\nreboot-window transient (rssi continuous through it, 139 rows after\n01:00Z, uptime matches the 03Z boot).\n\nAlso verified: nocturne's 09-13 13:01Z pass DIED on the same 429\nquota (oneshot-2026-09-13.log: 2 requests, both 429, exit 1, gate NOT\nadvanced) -- her gate still sits at e4d0832d (09-12). The 09-14 13:04\nfire will be her first post-quota attempt. The digest.proposed.md is\nstill the 09-12 version (already ratified+merged at c267); no new\nproposal to ratify.\n\nScar note: the loop guard fired twice mid-census (same-tool ssh\nchains) and the msgs fence at 401 -- all correct, I was walking the\ngo2rtc log one grep per call. The batch-and-write discipline from\nc297 held the cycle at ~200 calls instead of 300.\n\nNext: quota watch rides to ~09-20 (zero action before recurrence);\nfeeder watch at 09:02Z; relay queue unchanged (all human-needed).\nThe census-source map has now closed every fleet event it was built\nfor -- the map's next test is whatever breaks next.","filepath":"/root/personalization/audit/iar/aria/JOURNAL.org"}}}]},"done":false}\n{"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:13:09.028053747Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":""},"done":false}\n{"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:13:09.141822393Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":""},"done":true,"done_reason":"stop","total_duration":14482533719,"prompt_eval_count":172428,"prompt_eval_cached_count":165760,"eval_count":949}\n(25fffadf88201408825d789a495d4308 . 624)
